### 1. valid CA but NO client certificate (expect refusal)
$ curl --cacert ca.crt https://aggregator:8000/health
curl: (56) OpenSSL SSL_read: OpenSSL/3.5.5: error:0A00045C:SSL routines::tlsv13 alert certificate required, errno 0
 [HTTP 000] (curl exit 56)

### 2. client certificate from an UNTRUSTED CA (expect refusal)
$ curl --cacert ca.crt --cert rogue.crt --key rogue.key https://aggregator:8000/health
 [HTTP 000]curl: (56) OpenSSL SSL_read: OpenSSL/3.5.5: error:0A000418:SSL routines::tlsv1 alert unknown ca, errno 0
 (curl exit 56)

### 3. valid client certificate, NO token (expect TLS ok, then 401)
$ curl --cacert ca.crt --cert hospA.crt --key hospA.key https://aggregator:8000/health
{"ok": false, "error": "unauthorised"} [HTTP 401] (curl exit 0)

### 4. valid client certificate + token (expect 200)
$ curl --cacert ca.crt --cert hospA.crt --key hospA.key -H @token-header-file https://aggregator:8000/health
{"ok": true} [HTTP 200] (curl exit 0)

### 5. hospA's certificate posting as site hospB (expect 403: certificate CN must equal site_id)
$ curl -X POST --cert hospA.crt ... -d '{"site_id":"hospB",...}' https://aggregator:8000/stats
{"ok": false, "error": "site_id does not match the client certificate"} [HTTP 403] (curl exit 0)

### 6. TLS 1.2 client with a valid certificate (expect refusal: TLS 1.3 only)
curl: (35) TLS connect error: error:0A00042E:SSL routines::tlsv1 alert protocol version
 [HTTP 000] (curl exit 35)

### 7. plain HTTP to the TLS port (expect no HTTP response)
curl: (52) Empty reply from server
 [HTTP 000] (curl exit 52)

